Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:30:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] population: the periodic samples on odd days, never on a
 month tick (B3 P3)

The employment sample (every OCC_PERIOD = 4 days) and the demographics
sample (every DEMO_AGG_DAYS = 32) ran on phase 0: the employment sample
on every other month tick, the demographics sample (+0.5-2 ms at 1M,
up to 6 in frames) on one tick in 16. They now run on
day % 4 === OCC_PHASE (1) and day % 32 === DEMO_PHASE (17): odd days,
and a day of the month has the parity of its day number, so neither
lands on a tick (dom 0), on tourism's venue pass (26) or the advisors'
zone scan (28); 17 = 1 mod 4 keeps every demographics day an employment
day. The 'demographics' layer event moves from the tick to dom 1
(DEMOGRAPHICS_EVENT_PHASE): the overlay's refresh leaves the month
frame. No save state: the phases follow st.day after a load.

EQHQ_DAY, OUTAGE_PRUNE_DAY (the prune day, named), the phases and
DEMO_AGG_DAYS are exported for the calendar test.

The frozen J10 reference (tests/sim/exact/j10Original.ts) takes the same
phases and event day (its header says so). desirability.test.ts's saved
demographics sample test follows the new sample days (49, 81).
monthSpread.test.ts: the samples never on a tick and on their own days
only, the event on dom 1; the calendar of the month work.

Behaviour changes by design (the bot's output changes): the tick reads
an employment sample 1-3 days old.

